- Attribute fallback payouts through signed coin-to-mailbox links
  Recheck each link and the mailbox's registered destination before payout.
  Remove account-key discovery and hold outputs without a valid link.
  [#46](https://github.com/BullishNode/abandon-ship-bark/pull/46)
  - **BREAKING:** Use fresh stores and mailbox-only v4 registrations.
- Require signed ownership links before customer issuance
  Verify the actual output key at every admission and again in the tree writer,
  so an accepted customer coin has an authenticated bitcoin fallback destination.
  [#46](https://github.com/BullishNode/abandon-ship-bark/pull/46)
- Require fallback registration for every mailbox operation
  Refuse unregistered reads, subscriptions and notices before allocating a
  checkpoint or channel, and notify round recipients only after commit.
  [#46](https://github.com/BullishNode/abandon-ship-bark/pull/46)
- Keep fallback registration contention local to each mailbox
  Use the immutable mailbox constraint instead of a global registry lock, so
  one registration does not block unrelated admissions or mailbox operations.
  [#46](https://github.com/BullishNode/abandon-ship-bark/pull/46)
- Check forwarded destinations before invoice creation
  Verify the recipient's actual key, signed mailbox link and net amount before
  a new invoice or a Created-invoice retry. Keep the final claim checks.
  [#46](https://github.com/BullishNode/abandon-ship-bark/pull/46)
